WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
This intersection of computer science, AI,
and computational linguistics is

2
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.480
known as natural language processing.

3
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.200
It allows computers to analyze and
generate human text.

4
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:16.140
Large language models are a specific class
of AI trained on massive text

5
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.800
datasets to simulate human-like
communication.

6
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.700
Looking at this graphic, the core mechanic
is clear.

7
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.480
These models do not think. They operate
purely on next word prediction,

8
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.220
assigning statistical probabilities to
potential following words.

9
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.720
Chaining these guesses together outputs
coherent sentences, creating what we

10
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.860
call the illusion of understanding.

11
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:42.080
A large language model does not comprehend
language in the human sense.

12
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.100
It relies exclusively on mathematical
frequencies.

13
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.860
We must guard against anthropomorphizing
these systems.

14
00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:54.820
Assigning human intent, reasoning, or
factual comprehension to an LLM's output

15
00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.000
invites severe methodological and ethical
errors in research.
